# The clean-room example resolves fresh on purpose.
#
# A committed lockfile would pin the transitive tree, and the question this example
# answers is what a developer's FIRST install produces — including whatever npm
# resolves today. CI rewrites the SDK dependency to the tarball it just built, which
# a lockfile would also fight with.
examples/clean-room/package-lock.json
